stage: 1
finding: P1: PhysicsAssets.remove lowers _freeHandle and add reissues the identical handle (assets.ts:8-12,23-26); clear also resets allocation. An unchanged Shape.geometry therefore resolves to unrelated replacement geometry. Independently reproduced through shapeHullGeometry: handle 1, upper x 1 -> remove(1), add unrelated hull -> handle 1, unchanged Shape.geometry, upper x 9. This retains the silent-geometry-change class the stage was opened to close. Meshes has the same ABA fault (mesh.ts:135-140,150-158), not a justification; Bevy Assets increments generation on reuse (assets.rs:71-76). Smallest fix: monotonically allocate non-reused handles, including across ordinary clear, guard u32 exhaustion, snapshot/restore the high-water allocator; alternatively generation-checked handles. Add stale Shape and compound-child tests across remove/add and clear/add; existing tests explicitly require reuse and cannot protect this claim. P2: ShapeMaterials.add returns a zero-based handle but Shape.materialSet consumes handle + 1, with 0 silently meaning none (shape.ts:78; marshal-shape.ts:54-58). Thus the natural assignment materialSet: world.resource(ShapeMaterials).add(def) silently drops the first set and selects the preceding set for later handles. This is not Shallot's other optional asset convention: Sound.clip and StandardMaterial.baseColorTexture consume returned IDs directly and use -1 for absence. JSDoc and MIGRATION describe the offset accurately, but do not make the public seam self-explanatory. Smallest fix: direct material handle in an i32 field with -1 default/absence, update readers, consumers and migration, and test first and second material handles with distinguishable materials through spawn/sync/restore.
